0.2 Pipeline
?fig-pipeline lists the nine steps in the order the scripts run them. Steps 2 to 5 are Section 3.1; step 7 is Section 4.1; step 8 is 2.1, three regimes; step 9 is Section 5.1.
%%| label: fig-pipeline
%%| fig-cap: "Analysis pipeline, read left to right on each row. Row 1 builds the gene panel from the single-cell counts: quality control, a presence gate in every type, an omnibus count-model screen ranked by effect size, and a cross-platform filter fitted independently at each of the three matched pairs (single-cell 48 h, 72 h and 96 h against the standard-Wnt bulk at the same time). Row 2 estimates one covariance per type and time on the linear scale, with the tuning parameter of each estimator chosen by cross-validated held-out Gaussian log-likelihood, lifts the estimates to DeCovarT's moments and deconvolves the matched bulk at all three times. The dashed box is optional; it needs the covariances of step 7."
%%| filename: fig-pipeline
%%| alt: Two-row flowchart. Row one, left to right: 1 GSE229513 UMI counts and cell-type labels; 2 cell and gene quality control; 3 presence gate in every type; 4 omnibus deviance or quasi-likelihood screen, ranked by effect size; 5 bulk consistency filter fitted independently at 48, 72 and 96 hours, single-cell against standard-Wnt bulk at each matched time. An elbow arrow leads from step 5 to row two. Row two, left to right: 6 optional multivariate refinement by Fisher information or NSGA-II, drawn dashed with dashed arrows; 7 per type and time on the linear scale, shrinkage covariance as default, or graphical lasso, SILGGM or PLNnetwork, with lambda chosen by cross-validated held-out log-likelihood and nested cross-validation comparing the four; 8 lift to DeCovarT moments mu hat j and Sigma hat W j; 9 DeCovarT on the standard-Wnt bulk at 48, 72 and 96 hours, with a note that the early-Wnt bulk has no matched single-cell reference at any time.
\begin{tikzpicture}[
  node distance=5mm and 5mm,
  pstep/.style={text width=26mm, minimum height=22mm},
  num/.style={font=\footnotesize\bfseries, text=ink!70, anchor=south west, inner sep=0.8mm}
]
\node[dimbox, pstep] (s1) {GSE229513 UMI counts\\ and cell-type labels};
\node[box, pstep, right=of s1] (s2) {Cell and gene QC};
\node[box, pstep, right=of s2] (s3) {Presence gate\\ in every type};
\node[box, pstep, right=of s3] (s4) {Omnibus deviance /\\ quasi-likelihood screen,\\ ranked by effect size};
\node[box, pstep, right=of s4] (s5) {Bulk consistency\\ filter, 48/72/96\,h:\\ single-cell $\leftrightarrow$\\ standard-Wnt bulk,\\ each matched time};
\node[box, pstep, dashed, below=16mm of s1] (s6) {Optional refinement:\\ Fisher information /\\ NSGA-II};
\node[keybox, text width=56mm, minimum height=22mm, right=of s6] (s7) {Per type $\times$ time, linear scale:\\ shrinkage $\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Sigma}}$ (default) $\mid$ glasso $\mid$\\ SILGGM $\mid$ PLNnetwork;\\ $\lambda$ by cross-validated held-out\\ log-likelihood; nested CV compares the four};
\node[box, pstep, right=of s7] (s8) {Lift to DeCovarT\\ moments\\ $\widehat{\boldsymbol{\mu}}_{\cdot j}$, $\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Sigma}}_{W,j}$};
\node[keybox, pstep, right=of s8] (s9) {DeCovarT on bulk:\\ standard Wnt,\\ 48/72/96\,h};
\node[note, below=1.5mm of s9, text width=30mm, align=center, font=\footnotesize] (n9) {Early Wnt: no matched single-cell reference at any time};
\foreach \k in {1,...,9} {\node[num] at (s\k.north west) {\k};}
\draw[edge] (s1) -- (s2);
\draw[edge] (s2) -- (s3);
\draw[edge] (s3) -- (s4);
\draw[edge] (s4) -- (s5);
\coordinate (turn) at ($(s5.south)!0.5!(s5.south |- s7.north)$);
\draw[edge] (s5.south) -- (turn) -| (s7.north);
\draw[dashededge] (turn) -| (s6.north);
\draw[dashededge] (s6) -- (s7);
\draw[edge] (s7) -- (s8);
\draw[edge] (s8) -- (s9);
\end{tikzpicture}
Branches that were tried and dropped are not drawn: partial correlations by matrix inversion, the huge graphical lasso, penalty selection by EBIC alone, and exports on the log1p scale. ?sec-cov-stale lists the outputs those branches left behind.

%%| label: fig-suppinger-design
%%| fig-cap: "Design of the two GEO series. Left, single-cell GSE229513: cell line, then time slot; each circle is one slot, coloured by cell line (B-S blue, SBR grey). Right, bulk GSE229386: Wnt schedule, then time point; each rounded square holds three biological replicates. Thick outlines mark the single-cell slots used in this book (48 h, 72 h, 96 h). Dashed links join each of the three matched pairs: single-cell 48 h (both lines) with standard-Wnt bulk 48 h, single-cell 72 h (SBR) with standard-Wnt bulk 72 h, and single-cell 96 h (B-S) with standard-Wnt bulk 96 h. The early-Wnt branch has no single-cell counterpart at any time."
%%| filename: fig-suppinger-design
%%| alt: Two trees. Left tree, scRNA-seq GSE229513, splits into cell line B-S with time slots 48, 52, 56, 96, 108 and 120 hours, and cell line SBR with time slots 24, 36, 48, 60, 72 and 84 hours; slots are circles, blue for B-S and grey for SBR, with thick outlines at the slots used in this book: 48 hours in both lines, 72 hours in SBR, 96 hours in B-S. Right tree, bulk RNA-seq GSE229386, splits into a standard Wnt pulse at 48 hours and an early Wnt pulse at 24 hours, each with time points 48, 72 and 96 hours drawn as rounded squares with three replicates. Dashed lines join single-cell 48 hour (both lines) to standard-Wnt bulk 48 hour, single-cell 72 hour (SBR) to standard-Wnt bulk 72 hour, and single-cell 96 hour (B-S) to standard-Wnt bulk 96 hour, each labelled matched pair. The early-Wnt branch is labelled no single-cell match.
